[[],{"page":{"pageNumber":6,"width":595.276,"height":782.362,"rotation":0,"renderRotation":0,"structureRoles":{},"graphicsOperators":{"paintImageXObject":1,"constructPath":58},"captionStarts":[{"text":"F I G U R E 2 Decisional Conflict Scale","fontSize":8,"x":397.1338,"y":44.440399999999954,"width":139.1904,"height":8}],"headingCandidates":[],"lines":[],"graphicsBounds":[],"invalidGraphicsBounds":0},"captions":[{"page":6,"lines":["F I G U R E 2 Decisional Conflict Scale","scores obtained immediately after, and","2–4 weeks after the pre-test genetic","counseling. (a) Comparison of Decisional","Conflict Scale (DCS) scores (the higher","the score, the stronger the decisional","conflict) based on a written questionnaire","obtained immediately after counseling","between the video group (video viewing","and decisional support by healthcare","professionals; n = 29) and the face-to-face","group (traditional face-to-face pre-test","genetic counseling; n = 28). The mean ± SD","of the total DCS score in the video and","face-to-face groups were 23.01 ± 15.29","and 18.75 ± 14.17, respectively (p = 0.28).","(b) In the questionnaire obtained","2–4 weeks after counseling, the mean ± SD","of total DCS scores in the video group","(n = 26) and face-to-face group (n = 28)","were 29.33 ± 13.87 and 24.05 ± 14.35,","respectively (p = 0.14). The score in the","category of “effective decision” was","higher in the video group (31.01 ± 16.82","vs. 21.43 ± 16.09; p = 0.04 [mean ± SD]).","n.s., not significant."],"rect":[397.11780000000016,44.440399999999954,549.6226000000003,327.44039999999995]}],"tables":[]}]
[["page","lines",0],{"text":"6 of 9","fontSize":7,"x":45.6378,"y":21.38429999999994,"width":17.832499999999996,"height":7}]
[["page","lines",1],{"text":"|","fontSize":13.02,"x":69.84,"y":17.914300000000026,"width":1.6443000000000012,"height":13.019999999999982}]
[["page","lines",2],{"text":"NAKAMURA et al.","fontSize":7,"x":490.3618,"y":21.399799999999914,"width":59.23559999999998,"height":7}]
[["page","lines",3],{"text":"participants who underwent genetic testing, one was diagnosed","fontSize":8,"x":45.6378,"y":506.0001,"width":242.75280000000006,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",4],{"text":"with BRCA2 PV. No participants were diagnosed with BRCA1 PV","fontSize":8,"x":45.605800000000045,"y":519.0001,"width":242.80399999999997,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",5],{"text":"or BRCA1/2 VUS.","fontSize":8,"x":45.621800000000036,"y":532.0001,"width":63.60000000000001,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",6],{"text":"4 | D I S CUS S I O N","fontSize":10,"x":45.6378,"y":569.0001,"width":98.99000000000001,"height":10}]
[["page","lines",7],{"text":"This study was conducted to determine the effectiveness of a video","fontSize":8,"x":45.6378,"y":597.0001,"width":242.77599999999998,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",8],{"text":"educational tool in BRCA1/2 pre-test counseling in Japanese pa-","fontSize":8,"x":45.62980000000002,"y":610.0001,"width":242.7919999999999,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",9],{"text":"tients. Our tool significantly reduced the time required for pre-test","fontSize":8,"x":45.63779999999994,"y":623.0001,"width":242.78080000000003,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",10],{"text":"genetic counseling, with no significant difference in the decisional","fontSize":8,"x":45.6378,"y":636.0001,"width":242.78399999999996,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",11],{"text":"conflict.","fontSize":8,"x":45.6378,"y":649.0001,"width":28.996799999999993,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",12],{"text":"Although many alternative tools have been reported con-","fontSize":8,"x":58.6378,"y":662.0001,"width":229.80000000000004,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",13],{"text":"cerning pre-test counseling for BRCA1/2 genetic testing, there","fontSize":8,"x":45.65380000000002,"y":675.0001,"width":242.81200000000004,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",14],{"text":"are few reports from Japan and other Asian countries. American","fontSize":8,"x":45.67780000000005,"y":688.0001,"width":242.784,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",15],{"text":"reports may not be replicable in Japan because of their cultural","fontSize":8,"x":45.67780000000005,"y":701.0001,"width":242.78959999999995,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",16],{"text":"backgrounds and prejudice against hereditary diseases (Nakagomi","fontSize":8,"x":45.68580000000003,"y":714.0001,"width":242.80240000000003,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",17],{"text":"et al., 2016), as well as the preference to allow medical providers","fontSize":8,"x":45.70980000000009,"y":727.0001,"width":242.79679999999996,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",18],{"text":"to determine the appropriate treatment options (Slingsby, 2004;","fontSize":8,"x":306.9338000000001,"y":506.0001,"width":242.77600000000012,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",19],{"text":"Specker Sullivan, 2017). In our study, the DCS total score and sub-","fontSize":8,"x":306.9258000000001,"y":519.0001,"width":242.79199999999992,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",20],{"text":"scale scores obtained immediately after counseling tended to be","fontSize":8,"x":306.9338,"y":532.0001,"width":242.78719999999987,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",21],{"text":"higher in the video group, but the differences were not significant.","fontSize":8,"x":306.9337999999999,"y":545.0001,"width":242.788,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",22],{"text":"The DCS scores obtained in this study are comparable to the results","fontSize":8,"x":306.9337999999999,"y":558.0001,"width":242.7904000000001,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",23],{"text":"of previous reports (Christie et al., 2012), suggesting the validity","fontSize":8,"x":306.94179999999994,"y":571.0001,"width":242.79200000000014,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",24],{"text":"of the assessment methodology in this study. Herein, scores in the","fontSize":8,"x":306.9578,"y":584.0001,"width":242.78560000000004,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",25],{"text":"“informed” and “support” categories were similar in both groups,","fontSize":8,"x":306.95780000000013,"y":597.0001,"width":242.7879999999999,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",26],{"text":"indicating that the video educational tool provided sufficient in-","fontSize":8,"x":306.95780000000013,"y":610.0001,"width":242.77599999999995,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",27],{"text":"formation and that the subsequent face-to-face counseling effec-","fontSize":8,"x":306.9498000000001,"y":623.0001,"width":242.80799999999977,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",28],{"text":"tively supported the participants' decision-making. However, at","fontSize":8,"x":306.97379999999987,"y":636.0001,"width":242.79359999999997,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",29],{"text":"2–4 weeks after counseling, the “effective decision” score was sig-","fontSize":8,"x":306.98979999999983,"y":649.0001,"width":242.79199999999992,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",30],{"text":"nificantly higher in the video group, although there was no signifi-","fontSize":8,"x":306.99779999999976,"y":662.0001,"width":242.80000000000007,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",31],{"text":"cant difference in the total DCS scores. Q uestions in the “effective","fontSize":8,"x":307.0137999999997,"y":675.0001,"width":242.77199999999993,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",32],{"text":"decision” category ask whether one makes informed, value-based","fontSize":8,"x":307.0057999999998,"y":688.0001,"width":242.80240000000003,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",33],{"text":"choices and feels satisfied with one's choices (O'Conner, 1993).","fontSize":8,"x":307.02179999999976,"y":701.0001,"width":242.784,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",34],{"text":"One reason for the higher “effective decision” score in the video","fontSize":8,"x":307.0217999999997,"y":714.0001,"width":242.77360000000004,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",35],{"text":"group may be the influence of the video-viewing environment. A","fontSize":8,"x":307.0137999999997,"y":727.0001,"width":242.8000000000003,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",36],{"text":"F I G U R E 2 Decisional Conflict Scale","fontSize":8,"x":397.1338,"y":44.440399999999954,"width":139.1904,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",37],{"text":"scores obtained immediately after, and","fontSize":8,"x":397.1338,"y":55.440399999999954,"width":138.7312,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",38],{"text":"2–4 weeks after the pre-test genetic","fontSize":8,"x":397.1338,"y":66.44039999999995,"width":129.63759999999985,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",39],{"text":"counseling. (a) Comparison of Decisional","fontSize":8,"x":397.1338,"y":77.44039999999995,"width":144.50079999999997,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",40],{"text":"Conflict Scale (DCS) scores (the higher","fontSize":8,"x":397.1338,"y":88.44039999999995,"width":137.6703999999997,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",41],{"text":"the score, the stronger the decisional","fontSize":8,"x":397.1338,"y":99.44039999999995,"width":132.95679999999965,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",42],{"text":"conflict) based on a written questionnaire","fontSize":8,"x":397.1338,"y":110.44039999999995,"width":149.27119999999985,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",43],{"text":"obtained immediately after counseling","fontSize":8,"x":397.1338,"y":121.44039999999995,"width":137.3880000000002,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",44],{"text":"between the video group (video viewing","fontSize":8,"x":397.1338,"y":132.44039999999995,"width":144.0872000000001,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",45],{"text":"and decisional support by healthcare","fontSize":8,"x":397.1338,"y":143.44039999999995,"width":131.75119999999998,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",46],{"text":"professionals; n = 29) and the face-to-face","fontSize":8,"x":397.1338,"y":154.44039999999995,"width":149.30080000000015,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",47],{"text":"group (traditional face-to-face pre-test","fontSize":8,"x":397.1338000000001,"y":165.44039999999995,"width":138.47680000000008,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",48],{"text":"genetic counseling; n = 28). The mean ± SD","fontSize":8,"x":397.1338000000002,"y":176.44039999999995,"width":151.45360000000016,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",49],{"text":"of the total DCS score in the video and","fontSize":8,"x":397.1338000000002,"y":187.44039999999995,"width":138.9367999999996,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",50],{"text":"face-to-face groups were 23.01 ± 15.29","fontSize":8,"x":397.1338000000002,"y":198.44039999999995,"width":141.31279999999992,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",51],{"text":"and 18.75 ± 14.17, respectively (p = 0.28).","fontSize":8,"x":397.12580000000014,"y":209.44039999999995,"width":146.36400000000003,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",52],{"text":"(b) In the questionnaire obtained","fontSize":8,"x":397.12580000000014,"y":220.44039999999995,"width":116.79200000000003,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",53],{"text":"2–4 weeks after counseling, the mean ± SD","fontSize":8,"x":397.12580000000014,"y":231.44039999999995,"width":152.49680000000012,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",54],{"text":"of total DCS scores in the video group","fontSize":8,"x":397.12580000000014,"y":242.44039999999995,"width":136.46959999999967,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",55],{"text":"(n = 26) and face-to-face group (n = 28)","fontSize":8,"x":397.12580000000014,"y":253.44039999999995,"width":136.61760000000004,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",56],{"text":"were 29.33 ± 13.87 and 24.05 ± 14.35,","fontSize":8,"x":397.11780000000016,"y":264.44039999999995,"width":136.04239999999953,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",57],{"text":"respectively (p = 0.14). The score in the","fontSize":8,"x":397.11780000000016,"y":275.44039999999995,"width":138.96959999999984,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",58],{"text":"category of “effective decision” was","fontSize":8,"x":397.1178000000002,"y":286.44039999999995,"width":128.26959999999985,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",59],{"text":"higher in the video group (31.01 ± 16.82","fontSize":8,"x":397.1178000000002,"y":297.44039999999995,"width":142.87599999999986,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",60],{"text":"vs. 21.43 ± 16.09; p = 0.04 [mean ± SD]).","fontSize":8,"x":397.1178000000002,"y":308.44039999999995,"width":141.50639999999999,"height":8}]
[["page","lines",61],{"text":"n.s., not significant.","fontSize":8,"x":397.1178000000002,"y":319.44039999999995,"width":69.19919999999979,"height":8}]
